#. §0: `rfl`
#: Game.Levels.Strings.L01_Append
msgid "§0 (short for *reflexivity*) is the simplest proof there is: both sides are\n"
"literally equal once Lean computes them."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `step`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L01_Run
msgid "Use §0 to read the first symbol."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [NFA.path_cons_iff, DFA.evalFrom_cons]`
#. §1: `rw [← «{ih}» («{M}».step «{p}» «{x}»)]`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L11_DFAPath
msgid "Unfold both sides one symbol: §0.\n"
"Then turn the run on the right back into a path using the induction\n"
"hypothesis backwards: §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.NFA.L05_PathCons
msgid "Taking a path apart: one move"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{hq}»`
#. §1: `false = true`
#. §2: `cases «{hq}»`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L06_DeadEnd
msgid "§0 is a false concrete fact: the move table says §1.\n"
"§2 sees that no proof of it can exist and closes the goal."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `xⁱ`
#. §1: `xʲ`
#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L02_Pigeonhole
msgid "A finite DFA sends two different powers §0, §1 to the same state."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `u`
#. §1: `v`
#. §2: `u ++ w`
#. §3: `v ++ w`
#. §4: `DFA.evalFrom_append`
#. §5: `M.evalFrom q (u ++ v) = M.evalFrom (M.evalFrom q u) v`
#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L01_Indist
msgid "A DFA's only memory is its current state. So if two strings §0 and §1 lead it\n"
"to the **same state**, it can never tell them apart afterwards: whatever comes\n"
"next, §2 and §3 get the same verdict.\n"
"\n"
"This is the key to proving that some languages are **not** regular. You proved\n"
"§4 in the DFA world:\n"
"§5."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `cases «{h}»`
#. §2: `nil`
#. §3: `[]`
#. §4: `«{p}»`
#. §5: `«{r}»`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L04_PathNil
msgid "Take the path §0 apart with §1. Only §2 reads §3,\n"
"and it forces §4 and §5 to be the same state."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Subset.L06_Run
msgid "This is the second step you proved."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a`
#. §1: `b`
#. §2: `balanced = {w | w.count .a = w.count .b}`
#. §3: `aⁱbⁱ`
#. §4: `aʲbⁱ`
#. §5: `rw [balanced, Set.mem_setOf_eq]`
#. §6: `w ∈ balanced`
#. §7: `w.count .a = w.count .b`
#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L07_Balanced
msgid "**Final level of the game.** The strings with as many §0s as §1s are not\n"
"regular either.\n"
"\n"
"§2\n"
"\n"
"The same plan works, with the same strings: §3 is balanced, and §4\n"
"isn't. To unfold membership, §5 turns\n"
"§6 into §7. Then your counting results do\n"
"the rest."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{q}»`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L06_OnlyB
msgid "With no symbols at all, the machine stays in §0. This is true by computation."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [NFA.path_nil_iff] at «{hpath}»`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L04_Nil
msgid "A path reading nothing doesn't move: §0."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Strings.L09_ConcatUnion
msgid "**World complete.** You can now reason about strings and languages: membership,\n"
"union, intersection, equality and concatenation.\n"
"\n"
"Next: machines that *recognise* languages."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `L ∪ M`
#. §1: `M ∪ L`
#: Game.Levels.Strings.L07_Ext
msgid "§0 and §1 are the same language."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{f}»`
#. §1: `{M.start}`
#. §2: `«{hf}»`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L07_Accepts
msgid "§0 is reachable from §1: take §2 apart too."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Closure.L08_RegUnion
msgid "Regular: union"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `α`
#. §1: `σ`
#. §2: `M.step q x`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `q`
#. §5: `M.start`
#. §6: `M.accept`
#: Game.Doc.Definitions
msgid "A deterministic finite automaton over alphabet §0 with states §1:\n"
"\n"
"* §2: the next state after reading §3 in state §4\n"
"* §5: the start state\n"
"* §6: the set of accepting states"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `NFA.path_append`
#. §1: `NFA.path_append h₁ h₂`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L09_Glue
msgid "The arguments of §0 are in curly braces in its statement: Lean\n"
"fills them in from the two paths you give it. So you can just write\n"
"§1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `omega`
#. §1: `+`
#. §2: `-`
#. §3: `%`
#. §4: `/`
#. §5: `<`
#. §6: `≤`
#. §7: `=`
#. §8: `≠`
#: Game.Doc.Tactics
msgid "§0 proves arithmetic facts about natural numbers and integers: §1, §2,\n"
"numerals, multiplication by constants, §3 and §4 by constants, §5, §6, §7, §8.\n"
"It uses the arithmetic assumptions in your context."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `{a, b}`
#. §1: `AB.a`
#. §2: `AB.b`
#. §3: `.a`
#. §4: `.b`
#: Game.Doc.Definitions
msgid "The alphabet §0, with symbols §1 and §2 (or §3 and §4 when the type is clear)."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `AB.a == AB.b`
#. §1: `decide`
#. §2: `rw [if_neg (by decide)]`
#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L04_CountB
msgid "§0 is false, and §1 can show it:\n"
"§2."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L02_Pigeonhole
msgid "Finite memory, infinitely many strings: some information must be lost."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.NFA.L12_SameLanguage
msgid "Viewing a DFA as an NFA doesn't change its language."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `exact ⟨«{σ}», «{hσ}», «{M}».compl, DFA.compl_accepts «{M}»⟩`
#: Game.Levels.Closure.L03_RegCompl
msgid "Same states, the complement machine, and the last level's theorem:\n"
"§0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `M.step p x`
#. §1: `M`
#. §2: `p`
#. §3: `x`
#. §4: `M.Path p w r`
#. §5: `w`
#. §6: `p`
#. §7: `r`
#. §8: `NFA.Path.nil q : M.Path q [] q`
#. §9: `NFA.Path.cons : q ∈ M.step p x → M.Path q xs r → M.Path p (x :: xs) r`
#. §10: `q`
#. §11: `M.Path`
#. §12: `containsAB`
#. §13: `ab`
#. §14: `s0`
#. §15: `s1`
#. §16: `s2`
#. §17: `s0`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L01_Path
msgid "A **nondeterministic** finite automaton (NFA) may have *several* possible moves\n"
"for a symbol, or none at all. §0 is now a **set** of states: all the\n"
"places §1 may go from §2 reading §3.\n"
"\n"
"So there is no single run any more. Instead we talk about **paths**.\n"
"§4 says: reading §5, the machine *can* get from §6 to §7.\n"
"It is built by two rules:\n"
"\n"
"* §8: reading nothing, you stay where you are;\n"
"* §9:\n"
"  make one allowed move to §10, then continue.\n"
"\n"
"§11 is an **inductive proposition**: these two rules are the *only* ways to\n"
"prove it.\n"
"\n"
"Our machine §12 looks for §13 somewhere in the string. It has states\n"
"§14, §15, §16, and starts in §17."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L05_Exponents
msgid "Reading off the exponents"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `obtain _ | ⟨hq, hp⟩ := «{h}»`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L05_PathCons
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L03_NotS2
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L05_OneSymbol
msgid "Take §0 apart: §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `S`
#. §1: `x`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L05_OneSymbol
msgid "Paths from the next set = paths from §0 that start with §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `NFA.Path.nil q : M.Path q [] q`
#: Game.Doc.Definitions
msgid "§0: reading nothing, you stay put."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `[] ++ v`
#. §1: `v`
#. §2: `[]`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L07_Append
msgid "§0 is just §1, and reading §2 changes nothing. This is true by computation."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `step`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L01_Run
msgid "Nothing is left to read. One last §0 finishes the run."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L01_Indist
msgid "A DFA forgets"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `{u | u.length = 2}`
#. §2: `exact «{h}»`
#: Game.Levels.Strings.L02_Membership
msgid "Look at the assumption §0. It says exactly what the goal asks for,\n"
"because being in §1 just means having length 2.\n"
"Use §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `s0`
#. §1: `{s0, s1}`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L02_Track
msgid "In the same way, §0 is in this set too. The set is exactly §1: every\n"
"place the guesses could lead."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [Set.mem_compl_iff, DFA.mem_accepts, DFA.mem_accepts, DFA.compl_start, DFA.compl_evalFrom]`
#: Game.Levels.Closure.L02_ComplAccepts
msgid "Unfold everything: the complement, both acceptances, the start state,\n"
"and the run.\n"
"§0"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw`
#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L01_Indist
msgid "After the last rewrite both sides were identical, so §0 finished the proof by itself."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `parityA`
#. §1: `a`
#. §2: `ext`
#. §3: `DFA.mem_accepts`
#. §4: `parityA_evalFrom`
#. §5: `by_cases`
#. §6: `if_pos`
#. §7: `if_neg`
#. §8: `have h₂ : ... ∉ ... := by decide`
#. §9: `exfalso`
#. §10: `False`
#. §11: `exfalso`
#. §12: `False`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L11_Language
msgid "**Final level of this world.**\n"
"\n"
"§0 accepts exactly the strings with an even number of §1s.\n"
"\n"
"Everything you need is already in your inventory: §2, §3,\n"
"§4, §5, §6 and §7. In one case you will need\n"
"to show a state is *not* accepting: remember the pattern from the\n"
"counterexample level, §8.\n"
"\n"
"One new tactic: §9 changes any goal into §10. From a contradiction\n"
"you can prove anything, so when your assumptions contradict each other, use\n"
"§11 and then derive §12."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [Set.mem_inter_iff, DFA.mem_accepts, DFA.mem_accepts, DFA.mem_accepts]`
#: Game.Levels.Closure.L05_Inter
msgid "Unfold the intersection of languages and all three acceptances:\n"
"§0."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Subset.L04_Nil
msgid "Reading nothing, the subset machine's set is what's reachable by reading nothing."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h₂}»`
#. §1: `«{h₁}»`
#. §2: `«{h₁}»`
#. §3: `False`
#. §4: `¬ P`
#. §5: `exact «{h₂}» «{h₁}»`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L04_Counterexample
msgid "§0 says *not* §1, that is, §2 leads to §3. A proof of\n"
"§4 works like a function: §5."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Strings
msgid "Before building machines, we need what they read and what they recognise:\n"
"**strings** and **languages**.\n"
"\n"
"This world also teaches you the basics of proving things in Lean. Every level is\n"
"a statement; you prove it by typing *tactics*, one per line. The goal you still\n"
"have to prove is always shown in the middle of the screen."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `r`
#. §1: `M.toDFA.step S x`
#. §2: `xs`
#. §3: `r`
#. §4: `S`
#. §5: `x :: xs`
#. §6: `p ∈ S`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L05_OneSymbol
msgid "Second step. Reaching §0 from the *next* set §1 by reading §2\n"
"is the same as reaching §3 from §4 by reading §5: a first move from\n"
"some §6, then the rest of the path."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Closure
msgid "Which operations on languages keep them **regular**, recognisable by a DFA?\n"
"\n"
"In this world you'll build new machines out of old ones. You'll flip a\n"
"machine's verdict, and you'll run two machines side by side. Then you'll prove\n"
"that regular languages are closed under complement, intersection and union."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{M}».compl.accept`
#. §1: `«{M}».accept`
#. §2: `rfl`
#: Game.Levels.Closure.L02_ComplAccepts
msgid "Being in §0 means *not* being in §1, by definition.\n"
"§2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `by_cases h : «{w}».count AB.a % 2 = 0`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L11_Language
msgid "Everything depends on whether the count is even.\n"
"§0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `∃`
#. §1: `obtain ⟨q, hq, hp⟩ := «{h}»`
#. §2: `cons`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L05_PathCons
msgid "Take the §0 apart with §1,\n"
"then build the path with the §2 rule."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Subset.L07_Accepts
msgid "The subset construction is correct."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{hv}»`
#. §1: `«{v}»`
#. §2: `obtain hv | hv := «{hv}»`
#: Game.Levels.Strings.L09_ConcatUnion
msgid "§0 is an *or*. Which language §1 is in decides which side of\n"
"the goal you prove. Split it with §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rfl`
#. §1: `exact ⟨«{M}».step «{p}» «{x}», rfl, «{h}»⟩`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L11_DFAPath
msgid "Give the one possible next state. The move is allowed by §0:\n"
"§1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `ab`
#: Game.Levels.NFA
msgid "A DFA has exactly one move for every symbol. An NFA may have several, or none,\n"
"and it accepts a string if *some* sequence of choices works.\n"
"\n"
"In this world you'll build paths by guessing, take paths apart, and design an\n"
"NFA that finds §0 anywhere in a string. At the end you'll show that every\n"
"DFA is an NFA."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Closure.L08_RegUnion
msgid "The union of two regular languages is regular."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{w}» ∈ «{L}»`
#: Game.Levels.Strings.L05_Inter
msgid "First part: §0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [← h]`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L11_DFAPath
msgid "§0 rewrites right-to-left: it replaced the run by the path."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Closure.L09_SymmDiff
msgid "Regular languages are closed under symmetric difference."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{hq}»`
#. §1: `«{q}»`
#. §2: `rw [DFA.mem_toNFA_step] at «{hq}»`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L11_DFAPath
msgid "§0 says §1 is the only possible next state:\n"
"§2."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DFA.L02_Accepts
msgid "Accepting a string"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `s0`
#. §1: `containsAB`
#. §2: `s0`
#. §3: `s0`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L07_Wait
msgid "From §0, §1 can always stay in §2, whatever it reads. So it can\n"
"wait in §3 through any string."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `ab`
#. §1: `containsAB`
#. §2: `s0`
#. §3: `s2`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L02_Moves
msgid "Reading §0, §1 can get from §2 to §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `L ∪ M`
#. §1: `L`
#. §2: `M`
#. §3: `L ⊆ M`
#. §4: `L`
#. §5: `M`
#. §6: `L ⊆ M`
#. §7: `w`
#. §8: `w ∈ L`
#. §9: `w ∈ M`
#. §10: `intro w hw`
#: Game.Levels.Strings.L04_Subset
msgid "Languages can be combined like sets. §0 contains the strings in §1 *or* in §2.\n"
"§3 means every string of §4 is also in §5.\n"
"\n"
"To prove §6, take an arbitrary string §7 together with the fact §8,\n"
"and show §9. The tactic §10 does exactly this: it introduces\n"
"the string and the assumption."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `s0`
#. §1: `containsAB`
#. §2: `ab`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L07_Wait
msgid "Waiting in §0 is what lets §1 skip everything before the §2."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Closure.L04_ProdRun
msgid "Running the product = running both machines."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Strings.L04_Subset
#: Game.Levels.Closure.L06_Union
msgid "Union"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `M.toNFA`
#. §1: `M`
#. §2: `M.toNFA.step p x = {M.step p x}`
#. §3: `DFA.mem_toNFA_step : q ∈ M.toNFA.step p x ↔ q = M.step p x`
#. §4: `step`
#. §5: `DFA.evalFrom_cons : M.evalFrom q (x :: xs) = M.evalFrom (M.step q x) xs`
#. §6: `M.toNFA`
#. §7: `p`
#. §8: `w`
#. §9: `r`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L11_DFAPath
msgid "A DFA is an NFA that always has exactly one move. §0 is the DFA §1 viewed\n"
"as an NFA, with §2, a set with one state.\n"
"\n"
"§3\n"
"\n"
"You'll also need the rule that §4 has been using all along:\n"
"§5.\n"
"\n"
"For §6, a path is the same as a run: the path from §7 reading §8\n"
"reaches §9 exactly when the run does."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `have := replicate_eq «{hn}»`
#. §1: `omega`
#. §2: `«{hij}»`
#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L06_Anbn
msgid "Read off the exponents with §0, and §1\n"
"finds the contradiction with §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [if_neg «{h}»]`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L11_Language
msgid "The count is odd, so the run ends in the flipped start state: §0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `ext w`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L11_Language
msgid "An equality of languages: start with §0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `q.flip`
#. §1: `even.flip = odd`
#. §2: `odd.flip = even`
#: Game.Doc.Definitions
msgid "§0 swaps the two states: §1, §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `step`
#. §1: `List.replicate («{n}» + 1) AB.b`
#. §2: `rw [List.replicate_succ]`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L06_OnlyB
msgid "§0 can't see a first symbol in §1 yet.\n"
"Make it visible with §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{ha}» : «{i}» = «{n}»`
#. §1: `«{hb}» : «{j}» = «{n}»`
#. §2: `omega`
#: Game.Levels.NonRegular.L05_Exponents
msgid "§0 and §1. §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `s0 → s0`
#. §1: `«{x}»`
#. §2: `cases «{x}»`
#. §3: `rfl`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L07_Wait
msgid "The move §0 is allowed on both symbols, but Lean needs to know\n"
"which symbol §1 is before it can check. §2, then §3 twice."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a`
#. §1: `step`
#. §2: `step`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L02_Track
msgid "Read the §0 with §1, then finish the run with another §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `containsAB`
#. §1: `ab`
#. §2: `u ++ [a, b] ++ v`
#. §3: `s0`
#. §4: `u`
#. §5: `ab`
#. §6: `s0`
#. §7: `s2`
#. §8: `s2`
#. §9: `v`
#. §10: `containsAB_wait`
#. §11: `containsAB_ab`
#. §12: `containsAB_stay`
#. §13: `NFA.path_append`
#. §14: `u ++ [a, b] ++ v`
#. §15: `(u ++ [a, b]) ++ v`
#: Game.Levels.NFA.L10_ContainsAB
msgid "**Boss level.** §0 accepts every string that contains §1.\n"
"\n"
"A path for §2: wait in §3 through §4, read §5 from §6 to\n"
"§7, then stay in §8 through §9. You have proved each piece:\n"
"§10, §11, §12. Glue them with\n"
"§13.\n"
"\n"
"(§14 means §15.)"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `obtain`
#. §1: `obtain ⟨h₁, h₂⟩ := h`
#. §2: `h : A ∧ B`
#. §3: `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := h`
#. §4: `h : ∃ x, P x`
#. §5: `obtain ⟨u, hu, v, hv, hw⟩ := h`
#. §6: `obtain h | h := h`
#. §7: `h : A ∨ B`
#: Game.Doc.Tactics
msgid "§0 takes an assumption apart:\n"
"\n"
"* §1 for §2;\n"
"* §3 for §4, and longer patterns like\n"
"  §5 for nested ones;\n"
"* §6 for §7, giving two cases."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `M₁.inter M₂`
#. §1: ```
#. def DFA.inter (M₁ : DFA α σ₁) (M₂ : DFA α σ₂) :=
#.   M₁.prod M₂ {s | s.1 ∈ M₁.accept ∧ s.2 ∈ M₂.accept}
#. ```
#. §2: `s.1`
#. §3: `s.2`
#. §4: `s`
#. §5: `unfold DFA.inter`
#. §6: `M₁.inter M₂`
#. §7: `prod`
#. §8: `DFA.prod_start`
#. §9: `(M₁.prod M₂ acc).start = (M₁.start, M₂.start)`
#: Game.Levels.Closure.L05_Inter
msgid "§0 is the product that accepts when **both** machines accept:\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"(§2 and §3 are the two components of the pair §4.)\n"
"\n"
"§5 replaces §6 by its definition, so that theorems\n"
"about §7 apply. You'll also want §8:\n"
"§9."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DFA.L06_OnlyB
msgid "Induction is how you prove things about strings of every length."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `parityA`
#. §1: `¬ P`
#. §2: `P`
#. §3: `intro h`
#. §4: `False`
#. §5: `have`
#. §6: `have h₁ := h [AB.a]`
#. §7: `h`
#. §8: `a`
#. §9: `have h₂ : P := by ...`
#. §10: `P`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L04_Counterexample
msgid "Someone claims that §0 accepts *every* string. Show that they are wrong.\n"
"\n"
"§1 means *P leads to a contradiction*: to prove it, assume §2 with\n"
"§3 and derive §4.\n"
"\n"
